@startuml
title Classical RK4 simulation and diagnostic lifecycle

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor Caller

package dynamics {
  interface DynamicalSystem
  interface ExtendedHamiltonianSystem
}

package simulation {
  class InitialValueProblem
  class SimulationRequest
  class RK4 {
    +track_energy
    +progress
    +step_observer
    +integrate(problem, request)
  }
  component "Four-stage RK4 map" as StepMap
  component "integrate_fixed_grid" as FixedGrid
  class IntegrationStep
  class IntegrationData
  class SimulationRunner
  class Solution
}

package diagnostics {
  component "Centered map differences" as Differences
  class GCAreaSymplecticityObserver
}

Caller --> InitialValueProblem
Caller --> SimulationRequest
Caller --> RK4
Caller --> SimulationRunner : simulate(...)
InitialValueProblem --> DynamicalSystem
SimulationRunner --> RK4 : integrate
SimulationRequest --> FixedGrid : t_span, max_step, output_times
RK4 --> StepMap : k1, k2, k3, k4
RK4 ..> ExtendedHamiltonianSystem : optional [z, k] derivative
RK4 --> FixedGrid : advance callback

FixedGrid --> StepMap : complete main step\nobserve=true
FixedGrid ..> StepMap : off-grid shadow step\nobserve=false
StepMap --> IntegrationStep : main steps only
IntegrationStep --> GCAreaSymplecticityObserver : optional callback
GCAreaSymplecticityObserver --> Differences : map_state
Differences --> GCAreaSymplecticityObserver : local Jacobian

FixedGrid --> IntegrationData : sampled history and step_count
IntegrationData --> SimulationRunner
SimulationRunner --> Solution : validated physical history\nand read-only diagnostics

note right of FixedGrid
  Uniform main grid is independent
  of the requested output density.
end note

note right of IntegrationStep
  Snapshots and map_state use the
  physical state normally, or [z, k]
  when energy tracking is enabled.
end note

@enduml
